// Hmong (hmn) — White Hmong / Hmoob Dawb (mww), Hmong-Mien, tonal. Input = the Romanized Popular Alphabet (RPA).
// Referee: wikipron mww_latn_broad (RPA→IPA), filtered to single-syllable (White Hmong is monosyllabic), variants
// merged. `segmentJoin` strips the referee's per-phone spaces. Tones are Chao LETTERS on both sides → the backbone
// strips them (segmental comparison); the offglide (◌̯), nasal (◌̃), creaky (◌̰) and breathy (◌̤) marks are combining
// diacritics the backbone also strips. So the eval validates the SEGMENTAL backbone; tone + nasalisation are folded.
// single-source (wikipron mww, ~470 pairs; thin). RPA is deterministic so the converter generalises past it.
