    "secondaryGap": "Single source (wikipron mww, ~455 single-syllable entries — thin). No kaikki White Hmong / epitran mww. RPA is a deterministic phonemic orthography, so the authored maps generalise over unseen RIME/TONE combinations of known onsets (5-fold held-out CV 94.1%). BUT the referee attests only ~50 onsets; the remaining ~11 standard White Hmong onsets (nrh, rh, nph, nqh, nch, ml, hml, dl, dlh, ndl, ndlh) were SPEC-FILLED from the documented RPA tables (series-consistent, referee-unattested). An onset outside the map falls through as raw RPA — a real (not just breadth) reliability edge that neither the 100% nor the held-out CV can detect (both share the referee's onset inventory). The Green/Mong-Njua (hnj) variety + tone sandhi are deferred.",
